<BaseLayout title="Data Methodology" description="How Nursing Career Data sources, validates, and presents U.S. nursing wage information.">
<main><p class="eyebrow">Transparency</p><h1>Data methodology</h1><p class="lead">Our goal is to publish nursing wage information with clear definitions, source attribution, and reference dates.</p>
<section class="panel"><h2>Primary source</h2><p>We intend to use the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS) program for occupation-level wage and employment estimates.</p><p><a href="https://www.bls.gov/oes/">BLS Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics →</a></p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Measures</h2><p>Annual mean wage, annual median wage, hourly mean wage, and employment estimates are distinct measures. We will label each measure and will not substitute one for another.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Publication policy</h2><p>Each salary figure must have a source and reference period. Missing or unverified values will not be presented as factual salary estimates.</p></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
